#. Tag: author
#: horizon.docbook:3
#, no-c-format
msgid "<firstname>Jason</firstname> <surname>Harris</surname>"
msgstr "<firstname>Jason</firstname> <surname>Harris</surname>"

#. Tag: title
#: horizon.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Horizon"
msgstr "O horizonte"

#. Tag: primary
#: horizon.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid "Horizon"
msgstr "Horizonte"

#. Tag: seealso
#: horizon.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "Horizontal Coordinates"
msgstr "Coordenadas horizontais"

#. Tag: para
#: horizon.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <firstterm>Horizon</firstterm> is the line that separates Earth from "
"Sky. More precisely, it is the line that divides all of the directions you "
"can possibly look into two categories: those which intersect the Earth, and "
"those which do not. At many locations, the Horizon is obscured by trees, "
"buildings, mountains, &etc;. However, if you are on a ship at sea, the "
"Horizon is strikingly apparent."
msgstr ""
"O <firstterm>horizonte</firstterm> é a liña que separa a terra do ceo. Para "
"ser máis exacto, é a liña que divide todas as direccións nas que pode mirar "
"en dúas categorías: as que intersecan a terra, e as que non o fan. En moito "
"lugares, o horizonte está oculto por árbores, edificios, montes &etc;. "
"Porén, se está nun barco no mar, o horizonte é nidio."

#. Tag: para
#: horizon.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The horizon is the <firstterm>Fundamental Plane</firstterm> of the <link "
"linkend=\"horizontal\">Horizontal Coordinate System</link>. In other words, "
"it is the locus of points which have an <firstterm>Altitude</firstterm> of "
"zero degrees."
msgstr ""
"O horizonte é o <firstterm>plano fundamental</firstterm> no <link linkend="
"\"horizontal\">sistema de coordenadas horizontais</link>. Con outras "
"palabras, é o lugar xeométrico dos puntos que teñen una <firstterm>altitude</"
"firstterm> de cero graus."
